# Frontend Standards

- Build responsive UI from mobile upward.
- Keep components focused on one purpose; extract shared UI only when reuse is real.
- Use semantic elements for navigation, product lists, forms, buttons, prices, and status messages.
- Avoid placeholder marketing copy in committed user-facing screens unless the feature is explicitly a mockup.
- Handle loading, empty, success, and error states for catalog, cart, checkout, and order flows.
- Keep promotion logic separate from presentation so discounts can be tested.
- Prefer explicit product, cart, promotion, and order types over loosely shaped objects.
- Use CSS or the selected design system consistently once the stack is chosen.
